const schema = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Article","headline":"Zhangjiajie Glass Bridge | Grand Canyon Guide (2026)","description":"Complete guide to Zhangjiajie Glass Bridge: tickets, opening hours, how to get there, what to expect, and how to book the best time slot.","datePublished":"2026-07-01","dateModified":"2026-07-30","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Zhangjiajie Guide Team"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://zhangjiajie-national-park.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Glass Bridge","item":"https://zhangjiajie-national-park.com/glass-bridge/"}]}]};
---
<BaseLayout title="Zhangjiajie Glass Bridge | Grand Canyon Guide (2026)" description="Complete guide to Zhangjiajie Glass Bridge: tickets, opening hours, how to get there, what to expect, and how to book the best time slot." author="Zhangjiajie Guide Team" datePublished="July 2026">
<slot name="head"><script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}></script></slot>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 md:px-6 pb-20 md:pb-28">
  <div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-forest-200 bg-forest-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-forest-700 mb-6">Glass Bridge</div>
  <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 leading-tight">Zhangjiajie Glass Bridge</h1>
  <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">The world's longest and highest glass-bottom bridge: 430 meters across, suspended 300 meters above the Zhangjiajie Grand Canyon. Walking onto transparent glass with nothing but air beneath your feet is more unnerving than you expect.</p>
  <nav class="mt-6 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-stone-400" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/" class="hover:text-forest-700 transition-colors">Home</a><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 3l5 5-5 5"/></svg><span class="text-stone-600">Glass Bridge</span></nav>

  <div class="mt-12 space-y-12">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-4">Practical Information</h2>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 overflow-hidden"><table class="w-full text-sm"><tbody class="divide-y divide-stone-100"><tr><td class="px-5 py-3 text-stone-600 font-medium w-32">Location</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-stone-600">Zhangjiajie Grand Canyon, about 60 km from Wulingyuan</td></tr><tr><td class="px-5 py-3 text-stone-600 font-medium">Ticket Price</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-stone-600">CNY 128 (bridge only). Combo with canyon hike + boat: CNY 219</td></tr><tr><td class="px-5 py-3 text-stone-600 font-medium">Hours</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-stone-600">8:00 AM – 5:00 PM (last entry 4:00 PM)</td></tr><tr><td class="px-5 py-3 text-stone-600 font-medium">Time Slots</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-stone-600">8:00, 9:00, 10:00, 11:00, 12:30, 13:30, 14:30 — book online at least a day ahead</td></tr><tr><td class="px-5 py-3 text-stone-600 font-medium">Restrictions</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-stone-600">No selfie sticks, no drones, no large bags (free lockers available), no high heels</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-4">What to Expect</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">The bridge itself is a flat walkway with glass panels set into the floor. The glass is 6 cm thick and completely transparent — you can see the canyon floor 300 meters below. Walking onto it the first time triggers a genuine adrenaline response, even for people who are not afraid of heights. After a few minutes, the fear subsides and you start appreciating the view.</p>
      <p class="text-stone-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">We visited in April 2026 with an 8 AM time slot. By 8:30 the bridge was busy but not crowded; by 10 AM it was shoulder-to-shoulder. The experience is dramatically better with fewer people — you can stop, look down, and actually feel the height rather than being swept along by the crowd.</p>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5 text-sm text-amber-800">
        <strong>Important:</strong> Bring your passport. Like all Zhangjiajie attractions, the ticket is linked to your passport number. No passport = no entry. Camera phones are fine; professional cameras with large lenses may be restricted on busy days.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-4">After the Bridge: Canyon Hike</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">After crossing the bridge, you have two options:</p>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-800 text-lg mb-2">Option A: Canyon Hike (2-2.5 hours)</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">Descend into the Grand Canyon via a stone staircase. The trail follows a stream through narrow gorges, past waterfalls, and ends at a boat dock. The hike is mostly downhill but involves about 1,000 steps total. At the end, a short boat ride (included in combo ticket) takes you to the exit. This is worth doing if you have the time and energy.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-800 text-lg mb-2">Option B: Slide + Boat (1 hour)</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">A 600-meter slide (CNY 30) takes you from the bridge exit down to the canyon floor — it is genuinely fun and surprisingly fast. From the slide exit, a 10-minute walk leads to the boat dock. Less scenic than the full hike, but much easier on the knees. We did the slide in April and would choose it again over the hiking option unless you specifically want the canyon walk.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-4">How to Get There</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">From Wulingyuan bus station: direct minibus to Grand Canyon, CNY 25, 40 minutes. Departs every 30 minutes from 7 AM. From Zhangjiajie city: bus to Wulingyuan first, then transfer. Total ~1.5 hours. Taxi from Wulingyuan: CNY 80-100 one-way.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-stone-200 text-center"><a href="/attractions" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-forest-500 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-all hover:bg-forest-600 active:scale-[0.98]">All Attractions <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 3l5 5-5 5"/></svg></a></div>
</div>
</BaseLayout>
